# LC evaluation over tiles and streams · `spec:nrz:lc-evaluation-design`

**Principle (One original relation, indexed questions)** · `prin:nrz:lc-evaluation-contract`

This design instantiates (`spec:nrz:tiles-streams-design`) for the autonomous relation (`def:nrz:lc-relation`) and its grid and stream questions (`sec:nrz:lc-grid-questions`), (`def:nrz:lc-stream-standing-question`). A question is an exact projection of the original joint feasible set, lowered through bindings to masked heap computation, with new semantic facts admitted only at the barriers specified here. The decided ownership, cache, walk and flush positions remain (`sec:nrz:lc-grid-decisions`), (`sec:nrz:lc-stream-decisions`). CAS owns mathematical descriptors and checked decisions; it receives no heap values, storage tickets or mask bits. Bindings owns LC meanings and correspondence, matrix owns numerical regions, and the plan owner composes dependencies under (`prin:nrz:tiles-streams-contract`). All capabilities below are implementation obligations. Observations identify scoped source ingredients; implementation standing and LC completion belong to (`sec:nrz:lc-closing-register`), particularly (`tab:nrz:lc-closing-tiles-evaluation`). Limits, defaults and existing Work pins remain unchanged.

**Rule (General mechanisms have one authority)** · `rule:nrz:lc-evaluation-engine-reference`

Exact authority, executable templates and applications have the separate identities of (`rule:nrz:tiles-streams-identities`). This document supplies LC expressions, domains, recipes and absence laws; exact lookup and replay use (`def:nrz:tiles-streams-exact-key`), (`rule:nrz:tiles-streams-lookup-order`), (`rule:nrz:tiles-streams-replay`), lowering uses (`def:nrz:tiles-streams-lowered-lambda`), (`def:nrz:tiles-streams-lowering-key`), and execution uses (`def:nrz:tiles-streams-readiness`), (`rule:nrz:tiles-streams-walk-index`). Resource reservation, publication and retirement use (`rule:nrz:tiles-streams-residence`), (`rule:nrz:tiles-streams-barrier-publication`), (`rule:nrz:tiles-streams-release`). These mechanisms are not redefined by an LC question. Every native subgraph between the named barriers satisfies (`rule:nrz:lc-grid-fast-path`), including on a cache miss elsewhere in the graph.

## Question vocabulary and supported scope · `sec:nrz:lc-evaluation-vocabulary`

**Definition (Bound symbols and physical coordinates)** · `def:nrz:lc-evaluation-symbols`

Let i index one LC instance, j an observation or query sample, b an exact branch parameter tuple, and s the retained joint physical/source variables. Indexed input symbols are L(i,s), C(i,s), alpha(i,s), t(i,j,s), measured phase x(i,j,s), voltage amplitude V(i,s), current amplitude I(i,s) and E(i,s), with supplied/query roles rather than invented inputs for missing quantities. Alpha is the coherent radian coordinate of initial phase. Write P=LC, tau=sqrt(P), a=1/tau, omega=(1 rad)*a, phi=alpha+a*t and turn=2*pi for coherent-coordinate formulas. Bindings restores the exact units and difference roles of (`rule:nrz:lc-relation-kinds`); cyclic frequency f=a/(2*pi) and period T=2*pi*tau retain their distinct full-cycle relation (`rule:nrz:lc-cyclic-frequency-output`). An index has no physical time meaning without the epoch and clock maps. Each displayed operation denotes an original descriptor node and a checked numerical-law edge, not scalar descriptor construction during a loop.

**Definition (Question interface and returned family)** · `def:nrz:lc-evaluation-question-interface`

A checked LC question fixes the relation, all original declarations and repeated constraints, supplied and queried roles, epoch, index and physical domains, ordered source quantifiers, requested quantities and assurance, exact branch domain, boundary convention, supported recipe revisions and permitted refinement subgraphs. Outputs are indexed value symbols Q(i,j,b), their companion symbols, semantic domain/verdict nodes and masks resolving original associations. Unbounded branches are descriptor families with bounded requested numerical selections; unbounded physical values have explicit mathematical endpoints and no fabricated finite heap value. Projection coverage, nonemptiness, structural determinacy and numerical certainty are separate authority edges under (`rule:nrz:lc-relation-certified-sets`), (`def:nrz:lc-relation-determinacy`), (`def:nrz:lc-relation-certainty`). A branch box never declares independent coordinates or feasibility of every point in its Cartesian hull.

**Observation (Existing ingredients and their limits)** · `obs:nrz:lc-evaluation-source-boundary`

In `crates/bindings/src/lc_relation/forward/rectangle.rs`, `inverse_root` constructs a positive exact root and then requires `as_rational`; `forward.rs` additionally restricts the independent rectangle and nonnegative query time. These are the limitations in (`obs:nrz:lc-grid-square-refusal`), (`rule:nrz:lc-relation-forward-implementation`). In `crates/matrix/src/lc_relation/lower.rs`, family rendering calls `cover.arc`, exact index addition and literal decoding on the caller ledger; it is not the zero-exact-work tile pass. The scalar-inventory and Machin retention contracts are (`def:nrz:reuse-scalar-instance`), (`def:nrz:reuse-machin-instance`), not parameterized LC origin proofs by themselves. `crates/bindings/src/lc_relation/horizon.rs` retains the original source and explicit future coordinate; `calibrated_future.rs` checks original physical extremizers. Their scoped contracts are (`rule:nrz:lc-relation-reported-clock-horizons-implementation`), (`rule:nrz:lc-relation-calibrated-futures-implementation`), (`rule:nrz:lc-relation-broad-calibrated-futures-implementation`). Reusing these ingredients requires the family and live-binding obligations below. The inspection baseline and resulting statuses are maintained in (`obs:nrz:lc-closing-baseline`), (`sec:nrz:lc-closing-register`); these ingredients confer no implied evaluation or scale delivery.

**Decision (Enumerated initial realization)** · `dec:nrz:lc-evaluation-initial-subset`

The selected initial family fast-path contract requires the native-origin, Machin, positive-root-box, forward-rectangle, affine-lattice, positive-scale and quiescent recipes in (`sec:nrz:lc-evaluation-recipes`). Correlated recovery and calibrated future questions use the rational-fibre and future-extrema recipes only for their explicitly certified finite face/branch topology; otherwise they use the charged exact-certificate fallback. The implementation must support arbitrary arrived cell order on the layouts in (`sec:nrz:lc-evaluation-layouts`), without a pre-arrival sensor range. The contract includes generic positive nonsquare products through brackets and enclosed root evaluation; delivery is judged by (`claim:nrz:lc-closing-nonsquare-frequency`). Questions outside the supported grammar, including general nonlinear joint elimination, arbitrary source quantifier alternations, general atan2, clock drift, RLC and multiple-mode models, are refused as unsupported capability rather than approximated as solved questions. A false proposed alias-completeness certificate is refused as invalid evidence under (`def:nrz:decision-outcomes`). For a supported observation question, unavailable completeness proof instead retains the full candidate integer domain and every original constraint with `Undecided(UnsupportedCertificate)`; exhausted refinement or decision allowance retains that domain with `Undecided(RefinementExhausted)` or `Undecided(DecisionBudgetExhausted)`, as applicable. These unresolved outcomes follow (`rule:nrz:lc-evaluation-fibre-barrier`), (`rule:nrz:lc-evaluation-fallback`), (`rule:nrz:lc-relation-unresolved-implementation`), not capability refusal or a finite alias cutoff. The same observation family can remain unresolved under weak pi evidence and become certified under stronger evidence without changing its question or candidate-domain coverage. A sound outer projection may still be published with unresolved feasibility. This subset defines a capability contract under (`rule:nrz:lc-grid-acceptance-scope`); its implementation standing is recorded only in (`sec:nrz:lc-closing-register`).

## LC computation subgraphs · `sec:nrz:lc-evaluation-subgraphs`

**Rule (Exact preparation and dependency hoisting)** · `rule:nrz:lc-evaluation-hoisting`

Prepare the original relation, typed indexed declarations, exact one-radian/full-turn definitions, source equations, question/branch schemas, output inventories and all admitted operation/origin laws outside every tile. Reuse exact positivity, root, bracket, cover, cut, inclusion and outcome lemmas by their eligible content at barriers; newly data-dependent premises are not precomputed facts. Apply (`rule:nrz:tiles-streams-hoisting`) to numerical nodes: pi and its reciprocal share a prelude; fixed C, fixed phase, fixed energy, common source maps and source Jacobians share one evaluation when their complete dependencies permit. Frequency is shared across j when L/C do not depend on j. A fixed exact time or branch coefficient can share its import; a varying time, inferred rate or changed companion cannot. Exact preparation surviving flush and numerical prelude reevaluation after flush have the separate keys and lifetimes of (`def:nrz:tiles-streams-constant-key`), (`def:nrz:tiles-streams-prelude-key`). No tile repeats exact constants, definitions or proofs merely because its numerical inputs are new.

**Procedure (Forward frequency and period graph)** · `alg:nrz:lc-evaluation-frequency-graph`

Bind L(i), C(i) and their required companions. The positive-domain barrier (`rule:nrz:lc-evaluation-sign-barrier`) authorizes the native chain `P=L*C -> tau=sqrt(P) -> a=1/tau`; shared prelude factors then give omega, f and T. Bind P, tau, a, omega, f and T only when requested or needed downstream, with deterministic-total and numerical-error outputs before execution. The exact positive-root expression stays in the descriptor graph even when irrational. The bracket barrier (`rule:nrz:lc-evaluation-bracket-barrier`) is needed when subsequent exact cuts require rational coverage; a finite frequency enclosure alone does not choose a cycle. The energy barrier can independently classify rest without suppressing natural frequency. Hoist all fixed operands and authorized index-independent products under (`rule:nrz:lc-evaluation-hoisting`); retain the original LC equation in the omega/f publication under (`rule:nrz:lc-frequency-bundle-boundary`) where that existing statistical inventory is requested.

**Procedure (Forward phase and phase-series graph)** · `alg:nrz:lc-evaluation-phase-graph`

Bind alpha(i), t(i,j), a(i) and the joint timing/source maps. After positive-oscillation authorization, the native lambda computes `phi(i,j)=alpha(i)+a(i)*t(i,j)` with complete uncertainty propagation. Its barrier establishes the complete floor-cycle range and owned faces under (`rule:nrz:lc-evaluation-cycle-barrier`), then the selected native lambda subtracts the checked turn multiple, clips each arc to its owned cell and restores angle outputs Theta(i,j,b). The endpoint ownership is semantic evidence beside the numerical endpoint enclosure; roundoff cannot close an open face. A full-circle mask is a separate outcome of the width/coverage barrier, not a substitute for a wrap-crossing pair of arcs. An optional phase-threshold barrier follows these outputs under (`rule:nrz:lc-evaluation-predicate-barrier`). Share a, the full-turn prelude, exact wrap schema and fixed alpha across the sample axis. Signed query time uses the full product extrema, not the nonnegative endpoint shortcut in the existing forward adapter (`rule:nrz:lc-grid-root-brackets`).

**Procedure (Inverse phase-to-time graph)** · `alg:nrz:lc-evaluation-inverse-graph`

Bind the original joint alpha/rate family, target phase Theta_target(i), epoch and exact cycle domain. The cycle and feasibility barriers establish the complete candidate b and each admitted original fibre. For a requested member n, the native lambda computes `u=Theta_target/(1 rad)-alpha+2*pi*n`, then `t=u/a`, with positive reciprocal and correlated-family projection laws. Bind Time(i,n,b) and its companions before execution; a native reading of n has a checked exact-integer import enclosure and never determines n's identity. Independent alpha/rate boxes permit conservative interval arithmetic; a correlated fibre must retain its constraints and may have a wider outer enclosure until its projection law is available. Ordering uses exact endpoint separation, leaving overlapping members ambiguously numbered. The tail barrier (`rule:nrz:lc-evaluation-tail-barrier`) may publish a retained infinite suffix and a start-time symbol. The initial exact total-existence tail recipe is the nonnegative zero-phase rectangle of (`rule:nrz:lc-relation-time-queries`), (`rule:nrz:lc-relation-overlap-tail`); it does not extend the current member adapter to general signed inverse-time existence. Exact family/schema nodes, pi and any shared reciprocal of a are hoisted; finite rendering never discards the unrendered domain.

**Procedure (Observations to rate, product and initial phase)** · `alg:nrz:lc-evaluation-recovery-graph`

Bind observation arrays t(i,j), x(i,j), their independent supports, the original physical restrictions and shared-source symbols. A native preparation lambda encloses lifted strip coefficients and candidate extremizers. The alias/fibre barrier (`rule:nrz:lc-evaluation-fibre-barrier`) admits complete integer lifts and checked elimination of the original equations. On an admitted finite face topology, a native lambda intersects lower/upper faces, evaluates rate endpoints and conditional initial-phase endpoints, then computes P=1/a²; active-face changes requiring a new exact conclusion return to the barrier. For independent uncertain time with a>0, the exact law is `p_min-a*t_max <= alpha <= p_max-a*t_min`, with reconstruction in `[t_min,t_max] intersect [(p_min-alpha)/a,(p_max-alpha)/a]` under (`rule:nrz:lc-relation-timing-exact-implementation`). Division by a timestamp difference first requires a sign split; coincident times instead use their consistency constraints. Bound outputs Rate(i,b), Product(i,b) and InitialPhase(i,b) retain their joint fibre and common phase gauge. Hoist the observation-map schema, repeated exact sample-spacing relations, complete alias theorem where applicable, and exact source maps. Arrived readings and selected faces are not hoisted constants.

**Procedure (Element and scale projection graph)** · `alg:nrz:lc-evaluation-element-graph`

The recovered product/rate family feeds the positive-scale lambda after divisor and fibre barriers. With supplied C, use `L=P/C`; with supplied L, use `C=P/L`; with positive ratio R, use `L=R*tau` and `C=tau/R`; with energy and voltage amplitude use `C=2*E/V²` followed by `L=P/C`; with energy and current amplitude use `L=2*E/I²` followed by `C=P/L`. Bind L(i,b), C(i,b) and R(i,b) to outputs that share the same a, source and alias nodes. Simultaneous element restrictions keep `C in [C_min,C_max] intersect [1/(a²*L_max),1/(a²*L_min)]` and reconstruct L=1/(a²*C), with nonempty-fibre evidence before claiming attainment (`rule:nrz:lc-relation-joint-elements-implementation`). Extra supplied constraints remain conjuncts even if another equation provides a shorter computation. Hoist exact elimination identities and fixed scale factors; energy alone retains the free-scale family of (`arg:nrz:lc-relation-energy-identifiability`) with unbounded outputs where appropriate, rather than reserving a fake finite result tile.

**Procedure (Energy and amplitude graph)** · `alg:nrz:lc-evaluation-energy-graph`

For admitted positive elements, the native lambda evaluates `E=C*V²/2` or `E=L*I²/2`; supplied values from both expressions require the consistency barrier, not a choice that drops one. From E>=0 it evaluates `V=sqrt(2*E/C)` and `I=sqrt(2*E/L)`. With a restored instantaneous state the separate source-free energy lambda is `(C*v²+L*i²)/2`, retaining that state's original bindings (`step:nrz:lc-resonance-coordinate-lowering`). The energy barrier (`rule:nrz:lc-evaluation-energy-barrier`) selects positive oscillation or exact rest before any phase or V/I operation. Rest binds exact zero energy/amplitudes while returning undefined phase and ratio; a support spanning rest and positive energy retains both strata. Bound Energy(i,b), VoltageAmplitude(i,b), CurrentAmplitude(i,b) and requested ratio companions share all scale constraints. Hoist the half/twice factors and exact energy identities, and fixed energy only when its source/companion closure is invariant. This does not introduce voltage/current trajectory publication, whose closing boundary is (`claim:nrz:lc-closing-excludes-trajectories`).

**Procedure (Calibrated futures and horizons)** · `alg:nrz:lc-evaluation-future-graph`

Bind the retained observation family, shared clock offset d, shared phase offset s_phase, and any positive amplitude, energy or element gain fibres. The original equations retain `alpha+a*(r_j+d+delta_j)=x_j+s_phase+2*pi*n_j`; eliminating observations may use `gamma=alpha+a*d-s_phase`, but a future physical phase at reported r is `beta+a*r` with `beta=alpha+a*d=gamma+s_phase`. An actual-time future uses alpha+a*t. The fibre barrier checks restoration of every original measurement and physical restriction before the native future lambda projects the corresponding intercept/rate family. Its extrema feed the horizon barrier (`rule:nrz:lc-evaluation-horizon-barrier`); authorized finite thresholds lower to H(i,b) and companions, while infinite and undecided are explicit domain outputs. Hoist exact coordinate-change and extremum schemas and eligible prepared pi; never substitute gamma for beta or drop conditional calibration fibres. The closed narrow and broad future paths retain their own proof scope under (`rule:nrz:lc-relation-calibrated-futures-implementation`), (`rule:nrz:lc-relation-broad-calibrated-futures-implementation`).

**Rule (Driven sign consumers remain a separate experiment)** · `rule:nrz:lc-evaluation-driven-boundary`

An LC plan composing the existing driven question binds requested angular frequency, L/C and voltage under (`rule:nrz:lc-plan-bindings`), computes the original `X=a_drive*L-1/(a_drive*C)`, and passes its complete enclosure to the sign barrier. The later phase lambda imports exactly the selected positive or negative half-pi angle; a reciprocal/current lambda additionally requires a zero-excluding numerical divisor. Proved X=0 preserves successful zero impedance and independent autonomous outputs, returns undefined impedance phase and unavailable reciprocal/current; zero-straddling X retains the named unresolved continuation (`rule:nrz:lc-plan-undecided-continuation`). These signs concern impedance argument in (-pi,pi], not oscillation-phase floor wrapping. Exact original-expression authority and fixed coefficient nodes share the engine cache. General driven uncertain-L/C lineage and general atan2 remain outside this instantiation under (`claim:nrz:lc-closing-driven-lineage-boundary`), (`claim:nrz:lc-closing-excludes-general-atan2`).

## LC barriers, laws and exact keys · `sec:nrz:lc-evaluation-barriers`

**Definition (Common LC barrier key and outcome discipline)** · `def:nrz:lc-evaluation-barrier-key`

Write K_LC for the complete original question interface of (`def:nrz:lc-evaluation-question-interface`), original mathematical target and coordinate map, context/parent stratum, ordered quantifiers and actual proved domain, source/map assumption closure, exact origin/cut/cover/inclusion premises, selected conclusion and parameters, representation and law/checker revisions. Each barrier below specializes this content under (`def:nrz:tiles-streams-stratum-key`), (`def:nrz:tiles-streams-cover-key`), (`def:nrz:tiles-streams-outcome-key`); its proof identity separately includes the derivation. A mentioned key addition is never a replacement for K_LC. Heap versions and selections belong only to (`def:nrz:tiles-streams-attachment`). A failed membership check may mean another stratum or undecided, never the complement by default. Boundary intersection, missing proof, exhausted allowance, mathematical domain outcomes and malformed/stale evidence retain their distinct meanings under (`rule:nrz:tiles-streams-undecided`). All barriers freeze their demanded closure and publish by (`rule:nrz:tiles-streams-barrier-evaluation`), (`rule:nrz:tiles-streams-barrier-publication`).

**Rule (Sign, positivity and nonzero barrier)** · `rule:nrz:lc-evaluation-sign-barrier`

The exact partition for an original real target z is z<0, z=0, z>0; nonzero is the checked union of the two strict strata. For L, C, positive gains and reciprocal rate, only z>0 authorizes the corresponding LC operation. An enclosure with upper<0 or lower>0 supplies strict separation; equality requires an exact equality or an origin proving the singleton zero, not a rounded zero center. The key adds the original z expression, zero cut, sign/nonzero role and every divisor occurrence authorized by the consequence. A zero-containing enclosure with no equality remains undecided; a proven invalid physical element has a domain outcome, while a malformed descriptor or false certificate refuses. Refinement may tighten numerical enclosure, split a retained physical support with a checked cover, or invoke the exact-rational fallback. It cannot assume a positive nominal value. Flush uses (`rule:nrz:lc-evaluation-flush-local`) on every demanded value/companion, and never turns absent input into zero. Driven X uses the same partition with the distinct outcomes in (`rule:nrz:lc-evaluation-driven-boundary`).

**Rule (Positive-energy and quiescent-state barrier)** · `rule:nrz:lc-evaluation-energy-barrier`

The physical strata are `L>0,C>0,E=0,V=I=0` and `L>0,C>0,E>0,V>0,I>0` with the original energy equations. Negative energy or amplitude and incompatible zero/positive constraints are excluded only with original-domain evidence. The key adds the full energy/amplitude constraints, queried domain roles and exact rest/oscillation partition; a sign fact about E alone does not prove a complete feasible LC tuple. Selection of rest makes oscillation phase, its cycle and amplitude ratio undefined, without invalidating natural frequency. If uncertainty covers both strata, retain both branches and their domain outcomes; refine only to prove their coverage or unresolved membership, not to discard rest. Unsupported joint constraints refuse their adapter; unresolved feasibility remains explicitly undecided. Flush uses (`rule:nrz:lc-evaluation-flush-local`) and the fixed-inventory rule (`rule:nrz:lc-evaluation-flush-inventory`): absent observations cannot establish compatibility of a requested complete rest inventory.

**Rule (Positive-root rational-bracket barrier)** · `rule:nrz:lc-evaluation-bracket-barrier`

For the original P=LC, an authenticated origin gives rational outer bounds `0<p_min<=P<=p_max`. Candidate positive rational r,s certify `r²<=p_min` and `p_max<=s²`, hence `r<=sqrt(P)<=s` and `1/s<=a<=1/r` under (`rule:nrz:lc-grid-root-brackets`). The key adds the original product/root/reciprocal expressions, exact product enclosure, r,s, squared inequalities, positivity and derivation revision under (`def:nrz:tiles-streams-constant-key`). Correlated L/C use these as outer bounds only. Rational nonsquares are supported; the bracket never replaces the radical expression or proves endpoint attainment. Failed squared inequalities reject that proposal; unavailable positive separation stays undecided or the applicable domain outcome. Refinement runs a bounded native bracket-proposal/tightening lambda and rechecks its rational certificate, or tightens pi separately when a later cut needs it. Overlap with a cycle face retains all candidate branches. Exact irrational-face equality requires a separate identity. Flush uses (`rule:nrz:lc-evaluation-flush-local`) with current inputs and remaining allowance; no missing product gets an invented bracket.

**Rule (Cycle, phase-branch and complete-cover barrier)** · `rule:nrz:lc-evaluation-cycle-barrier`

For oscillation phase use `y=phi/(2*pi)` and floor cells `n<=y<n+1`, n an exact signed integer, with representative `phi-2*pi*n` in [0,2*pi). Check the endpoint floors of a justified lifted interval and retain every intervening integer; a closed lifted endpoint exactly on a face belongs to the next cell and can create its singleton arc. The key adds y's original lift, period definition, exact integer tuple/range, floor convention, owned arc faces and endpoint/complete-cover evidence. Observation lifts additionally retain each original equation and the complete alias domain, not just the selected n. Bracket/interval overlap cannot choose one floor: keep a conservative candidate cover with undecided selection, or refine via the bracket/pi and phase lambdas and checked subdivision. Nearest-cell [-pi,pi) and driven argument (-pi,pi] conventions require their distinct exact map and cut keys (`rule:nrz:lc-sign-axis-quantity-boundary`). Noninteger parameters, changed epoch or incomplete asserted covers refuse. Flush follows (`rule:nrz:lc-evaluation-flush-local`) for local phase and (`rule:nrz:lc-evaluation-flush-inventory`) for observation aliases; it never clips the mathematical integer domain to materialized members.

**Rule (Joint fibre, feasibility and structural-verdict barrier)** · `rule:nrz:lc-evaluation-fibre-barrier`

This barrier decides the original conjunction of lifted phase equations, measurement equations, positivity and every supplied interval. Exact cuts include active affine-face comparisons, nonempty conditional intersections, all-cycle contradictions and the proved free-scale or alias cardinality of the requested projection. Its key adds the ordered observation inventory, integer/gauge domain, all elimination/restoration maps, chosen active-face topology, retained conditional source fibres, witness/existence or emptiness statement and structural query. Outer relaxed strips prove coverage only. Nonemptiness needs an original full tuple or parameterized existence map; impossible needs exclusion of all admissible branches; determination needs whole-family structural evidence under (`rule:nrz:lc-relation-feasibility-witness`), (`def:nrz:lc-relation-determinacy`). A rejected candidate or failed adapter is not emptiness. Refinement may select finer joint faces, add checked original constraints, or retain all integer candidates with unresolved obligations. Unsupported simultaneous calibrations or quantifier structures refuse that capability without manufacturing independent sources. Flush uses (`rule:nrz:lc-evaluation-flush-inventory`); an incomplete fixed inventory cannot silently become a smaller solved question.

**Rule (Inverse ordering and overlap-tail barrier)** · `rule:nrz:lc-evaluation-tail-barrier`

For the exact-zero independent rectangle let `w=a_max-a_min`. With w>0 the cut is `n*w>=a_min`; the first tail index N has `(N-1)*w<a_min<=N*w`. This proves every later adjacent pair touches or overlaps, with start `2*pi*N/a_max`; equality counts as overlap. The key adds the original time family, rate bounds, zero-phase/epoch premises, nonnegative index domain, exact N, minimality and continued-overlap proof, plus separate total-existence evidence when asserted. With w=0 and starting/target phase fixed, retain the complete discrete family and no finite connected tail. General ordering compares original time-interval endpoints and preserves ties/ambiguity. An outer connected union supports only the weaker possible-everywhere status of (`conv:nrz:lc-relation-tail-status`). Refinement may tighten endpoints or the rate family using checked inclusion; exhausted threshold search keeps the full candidate family, never a truncated suffix. Flush uses (`rule:nrz:lc-evaluation-flush-family`); absence of unrequested numerical members has no effect on an already proved infinite family, while missing premises leave its tail undecided.

**Rule (Horizon and whole-circle certainty barrier)** · `rule:nrz:lc-evaluation-horizon-barrier`

The question names its future coordinate and safe reference r_ref. A supported extremum recipe proves for every r>=r_ref the exact lifted image or an explicitly outer interval `[l0+l1*r,u0+u1*r]`. Set `d=u0-l0`, `w=u1-l1`; the exact cut is `d+w*r>=2*pi`. With w>0 the eventual threshold is `max(r_ref,(2*pi-d)/w)`. With w=0 and d<2*pi it is infinite; with w=0 and d>=2*pi it is r_ref. These alternatives require exact sign/comparison evidence, including equality; an unsupported or changing future face needs a new proved piecewise-extrema continuation. A full hull alone establishes loss of exclusion by that outer cover, not realizability of every phase. The stronger physical whole-circle horizon needs a continuous complete image and original extremizers or equivalent existence proof (`rule:nrz:lc-relation-forward-horizon`). The key adds future coordinate, reference, extrema law valid on the entire future ray, affine coefficients or full piecewise cover, full-turn authority, claim strength and source fibres. Unknown width sign, incomplete extrema or uncertain cut remain undecided; an inadmissibly early reference, false source identity or unsupported projection refuses. Refinement keeps old coverage and common-reference inclusion under (`rule:nrz:lc-evaluation-refinement-barrier`). Flush uses (`rule:nrz:lc-evaluation-flush-inventory`) for required evidence and (`rule:nrz:lc-evaluation-flush-family`) for future claims; closing arrivals supplies no theorem about future source evolution.

**Rule (A branch horizon keeps its branch scope)** · `rule:nrz:lc-evaluation-horizon-union`

H(i,b) describes the retained physical branch b. A whole-question H(i) requires evidence for the complete union of admissible branches and its image at every later time; neither a minimum nor a maximum of individual branch thresholds automatically proves the earliest whole-family threshold. Common integer phase gauges may be identified only through their checked equal wrapped image. Other finite or infinite alias families retain their full union and unresolved horizon obligations until an admitted union/existence law settles them. In particular, loss of exclusion in an outer hull of disconnected phase images is not a physical whole-circle theorem. The horizon key and flush outcome preserve this branch-versus-union scope under (`rule:nrz:lc-evaluation-horizon-barrier`), (`rule:nrz:lc-evaluation-flush-family`).

**Rule (Predicate and quantified certainty barrier)** · `rule:nrz:lc-evaluation-predicate-barrier`

A predicate is an exact LC output relation such as Theta<theta_cut on a declared chart, an energy threshold or a specified horizon comparison. Its partition fixes strict/inclusive/equality ownership before execution. The key adds threshold expression and units, chart and wrap map, ordered index/source quantifiers, actual domain version and proof strength to K_LC. For a universal inner physical claim, complete cover inclusion proves yes and a feasible original counterexample proves no; for an existential inner claim, an original witness proves yes and complete exclusion proves no (`def:nrz:lc-grid-predicate`). Numerical enclosure overlap alone settles neither. A tiled refinement may tighten the same target, split the joint domain with a cover or seek a checked witness; unsupported predicates and reordered quantifiers refuse. Local decisions flush under (`rule:nrz:lc-evaluation-flush-local`); observed-domain, fixed-window and common-source aggregates use (`rule:nrz:lc-evaluation-flush-aggregate`). Their missing-data conclusions keep the requested quantifier order.

**Rule (Refinement and supersession barrier)** · `rule:nrz:lc-evaluation-refinement-barrier`

A refinement selects a new joint domain S_new only after proving `S_new subset S_old` for the same original question and coordinate maps. Its key includes both complete endpoints, directed inclusion, original repeated declarations, branch correspondence and the nonemptiness or witness-persistence premises of the transported claim under (`def:nrz:tiles-streams-cover-key`). The numerical child projects S_new and intersects the previous outer output with checked same-target evidence when needed. Valid universal coverage survives restriction; an existential witness or counterexample survives only if it remains feasible. Nonempty refinement cannot move the physical certainty horizon earlier at the same future reference; empty refinement publishes impossibility and no new physical horizon (`req:nrz:lc-relation-refinement-monotonicity`). Failed solving preserves the old theorem, complete refined candidate question and spent allowance. Widened support or changed readings without inclusion create supersession, not refinement. Flush propagates to any finite child and its demands under (`rule:nrz:lc-evaluation-flush-refinement`); it grants no new attempts.

## Supported origin and membership recipes · `sec:nrz:lc-evaluation-recipes`

**Definition (LC recipe application contract)** · `def:nrz:lc-evaluation-recipe-contract`

Each recipe is a closed mathematical lambda with typed varying parameters, exact input-family premises P, a proved original-target enclosure origin E, a cached stratum S and a cut from S to the claimed result. Its theorem is the scoped implication of (`def:nrz:tiles-streams-membership-recipe`); ordered law composition and all strict faces are part of the statement. A recipe's key combines its origin, containment and cut identities, representation and revisions; a live application supplies the authenticated source/companion selections separately. Native containment compares outward result bounds against representable bounds directed into S; a strict face requires strict separation. If that comparison cannot safely implement the exact predicate, it falls back to exact rational evidence. A successful scan creates a new scoped application/attachment and masks under (`rule:nrz:tiles-streams-barrier-cache`), without re-proving the family theorem. This contract is an owner proof obligation: changing the certificate's input endpoints does not turn an existing ground scalar inventory into a quantified recipe.

**Definition (Native-origin recipe)** · `def:nrz:lc-evaluation-native-origin`

The supported origin grammar is finite acyclic composition of admitted normalization/restoration maps, constant import, addition, subtraction, multiplication, squaring, positive square root, sign-separated reciprocal/division, and outward min/max or interval intersection with their domain laws. Each operation keeps its ordered inputs and shared-source occurrences. The family theorem quantifies over represented centers and nonnegative deterministic-total/numerical-error companions under the admitted binary format and arithmetic revision; it relates their mathematical decoding and original source maps to the reported enclosure. Numerical error is already included once in deterministic total, with the separate numerical-only channel retained (`rule:nrz:descriptor-binding-error-composition`). Original source uncertainty is an assumption with declared scope, not inferred from covariance. Existing checked scalar inventories in (`def:nrz:reuse-scalar-instance`) provide ground replay and law-order precedents; lifting their ordered laws to this family is required before native membership can discharge its exact premises. Unsupported operations or unbounded support cannot acquire a finite enclosure through this recipe.

**Definition (Machin and constant recipe)** · `def:nrz:lc-evaluation-machin-recipe`

The exact pi authority is the checked Machin certificate with its term counts, partial sums, signed remainder and exact bounds, using (`def:nrz:reuse-machin-instance`) and (`def:nrz:tiles-streams-constant-key`). Exact full-turn, half-pi, reciprocal-pi and admitted rational factors cite that authority and their original expression/domain checks. Numerical imports are prelude values with their own enclosures and errors, shared under (`def:nrz:tiles-streams-prelude-key`). Membership may use the proved pi bounds in an affine cut but cannot infer a new certificate from equal rounded endpoints. Repeated eligible exact preparation is a charged authenticated hit with no full finite-sum validation; a new numerical import after flush is charged separately. A tighter certificate has different content, and any consumer requiring stronger bounds must check them. Unsupported transcendental constants keep their named refusal rather than decimal substitution.

**Definition (Positive-root-box recipe)** · `def:nrz:lc-evaluation-root-recipe`

Quantify over positive L/C whose authenticated product enclosure lies in a fixed rational stratum `[p_min,p_max]` with the squared bracket premises of (`rule:nrz:lc-evaluation-bracket-barrier`). The recipe proves the product/root/reciprocal enclosure of the original frequency expression for every member. Its current native membership test checks the whole product enclosure against that stratum using the native-origin law, not just its center. Cached r,s and cut evidence can therefore serve many different nonsquare values and arrivals. When the product leaves that cached stratum, select another proved stratum or construct a charged new bracket; no sensor-range refusal follows from that miss. Root positivity and inverse monotonicity give coverage, while realization of the extremal bracket values is not asserted. The exact square case is a simplification of this same law, not a separate admission tier.

**Definition (Forward-rectangle recipe)** · `def:nrz:lc-evaluation-forward-recipe`

The initial forward origin quantifies over independent positive L/C intervals, a lifted initial-phase interval, a finite query-time interval and either positive oscillation premises or a separate rest branch. It intersects repeated original declarations first and refuses any additional constraint it cannot retain. Product extrema and the root recipe enclose a. For signed time the lifted bounds are alpha_min plus the minimum, and alpha_max plus the maximum, of the four products of rate and time endpoints. Independence permits these rectangular extrema; correlated sources retain the same calculation only as outer coverage. This generalizes the coverage portion of (`rule:nrz:lc-relation-forward-implementation`) without assuming its rational-rate or nonnegative-time restriction. A complete-image claim additionally needs a checked original reconstruction such as `L=max(L_min,P/C_max), C=P/L` for admissible P and compatible amplitudes/energy, with interval attainment and phase/time continuity proved. Cached box membership alone never grants that converse. The native lambda computes each cell's own enclosure; the shared rectangle is authority, not the returned answer for every cell.

**Definition (Affine-lattice recipe)** · `def:nrz:lc-evaluation-lattice-recipe`

Compose native-origin or forward-rectangle origin with exact affine full-turn cuts. A fixed n stratum proves `2*pi*n<=phi<2*pi*(n+1)`; a complete finite range uses checked endpoint floor predicates and union/owned-face evidence. The integer parameter may remain a binder with checked exact domain, so one theorem covers many requested n without treating a float as an integer proof. An application imports the requested bounded integer selections with certified error outside the kernel pass and keeps their exact association; arbitrary large or unrepresentable selections retain the family and report materialization refusal. Open-face equality fails a native strict test and uses exact equality evidence or remains undecided. The same grammar admits sign and threshold cuts on enclosed real LC outputs and the rectangular overlap inequality, with their distinct targets and proof keys. It does not prove completeness of arbitrary observation alias proposals; those require the original observation-domain proof under (`rule:nrz:lc-relation-cycle-branches`).

**Definition (Positive-scale and quiescent recipes)** · `def:nrz:lc-evaluation-scale-recipe`

The positive-scale family is the finite algebraic grammar in (`alg:nrz:lc-evaluation-element-graph`), (`alg:nrz:lc-evaluation-energy-graph`), with original energy equations, positive divisor premises and zero-excluding enclosure comparisons explicit. Its closed elimination identities justify each direction; monotonic endpoint bounds provide coverage and retained conditional parameter maps provide feasibility only when proved. The quiescent recipe instead fixes E=V=I=0 with positive elements, preserves every supplied independent timestamp interval, and has no phase, cycle or V/I numeric output (`rule:nrz:lc-relation-quiescent-inventory-implementation`). It may reuse the generic root recipe for natural frequency without extending any unsupported observed-rest calibration adapter. A physical box containing both rest and oscillation uses their covered union; it is not admitted wholesale to either recipe. These recipes share constants and laws, while native membership, branch masks and attachments remain per application.

**Definition (Rational-fibre recipe and finite topology)** · `def:nrz:lc-evaluation-fibre-recipe`

The supported correlation fragment retains finite rational affine strips in phase/intercept and positive rate, their original integer lifts, positive monomial scale maps, and additive offsets or positive gains with explicitly retained conditional interval intersections. It admits independent timing, a common clock, a common phase offset, repeated single-channel amplitude or energy readings, and element-calibration constraints only in combinations for which complete original elimination and reconstruction are checked, as delimited by (`rule:nrz:lc-relation-timing-exact-implementation`), (`rule:nrz:lc-relation-timing-both-implementation`), (`rule:nrz:lc-relation-three-shared-errors-implementation`), (`rule:nrz:lc-relation-energy-calibration-implementation`), (`rule:nrz:lc-relation-coupled-element-calibration-implementation`). This is a tagged union of proved combinations, not their unrestricted Cartesian composition. A fast family lambda fixes finite face incidence, branch coverage, denominator signs and active comparison strata; its parameters may vary only within those proved strata. Gain reconstruction keeps `G intersect [M/X_max,M/X_min]` for positive common reading support X and physical magnitude M; clock/phase reconstruction keeps their original coupled fibres. Distinct arrived face coefficients may need new exact applications or complete certificates. Without a proved parameterized topology, the same algorithms supply charged barrier evidence through the fallback, not an alleged family cache hit. Unsupported nonlinear fibres remain open or refused; marginal hulls cannot establish joint witnesses.

**Definition (Future-extrema recipe)** · `def:nrz:lc-evaluation-future-recipe`

An admitted future recipe proves that its retained lower and upper intercept/rate extremizers govern the whole ray from the declared reference. For a convex recovered phase/rate polygon, the face-order and monotonicity argument after the observation window yields affine extremes under (`rule:nrz:lc-relation-horizon-implementation`). For a reported clock use beta, with common-offset and calibrated-phase restoration under (`rule:nrz:lc-relation-reported-clock-horizons-implementation`), (`rule:nrz:lc-relation-broad-calibrated-futures-implementation`). The exact lemma retains both original extremizer witnesses and, for full-image claims, the interpolation or equivalent total-existence map. Native bounds on coefficients alone prove only an outer future cover. Membership checks the original finite topology and all conditional restrictions, then the horizon cut applies. A changed future reference, branch family or calibration composition needs its own authority; one past sample and an affine-looking numerical fit never establish this recipe.

**Rule (Calibrated future origin retains conditional offsets)** · `rule:nrz:lc-evaluation-calibrated-origin`

For the broad calibrated recipe at a fixed positive a, let G(a) be the measured gamma interval, S_phase the shared phase-offset support, A the physical initial-phase support and D the surviving shared-clock support. The physical reported-intercept image is `B(a)=(G(a)+S_phase) intersect (A+a*D)`, omitting the A restriction when it is absent. Selecting beta in B(a) retains `s_phase in S_phase intersect (beta-G(a))`, `alpha in A intersect (beta-a*D)` and `d=(beta-alpha)/a`. These are conditional fibres, not independent marginal selections. This broad law requires every original physical phase strip to contain the measured-plus-offset image; narrower physical restrictions retain their additional measured and physical strips and their checked common-offset elimination instead (`rule:nrz:lc-relation-narrower-clock-phase-implementation`), (`rule:nrz:lc-relation-broad-calibrated-futures-implementation`). The future-extrema law checks all applicable observation and clock-face slopes at its safe reference before choosing endpoint rates. Independent timestamp errors remain only in the variants whose original joint proof includes them; a future reported reading adds no fresh sample error without a separate declared query model. Current membership checks the same original restrictions and topology before the cached origin can authorize a horizon.

**Rule (Exact-rational fallback and honest unsupported outcomes)** · `rule:nrz:lc-evaluation-fallback`

When a family recipe is unavailable or its containment is inconclusive, a barrier may export mathematical rational enclosure endpoints with a complete scalar-origin inventory, exact expression/source correspondence and required cut or joint certificates. Bindings constructs this certificate, and CAS independently checks it through the existing scalar, constant and decision mechanisms; no raw heap entry is imported as an exact LC input (`rule:nrz:tiles-streams-key-boundary`). Each fresh certificate and comparison pays its actual Work and storage, including when all cells choose the same branch. Checked identical certificates can hit their full content keys. Exact rational arithmetic can certify squared brackets, rational affine faces and supported pi bounds; it is not a universal solver for transcendental equality, arbitrary joint fibres or unbounded aliases. A question outside the supported grammar refuses as unsupported capability; wrong meanings, stale bindings and false proposed certificates refuse as invalid evidence. For a supported observation question whose alias-completeness proof is unavailable, retain the full candidate integer domain, original constraints and last valid enclosures with `Undecided(UnsupportedCertificate)`. Exhaustion retains the same candidates and evidence with `Undecided(RefinementExhausted)` or `Undecided(DecisionBudgetExhausted)`, according to the exhausted allowance, under (`def:nrz:decision-outcomes`), (`rule:nrz:tiles-streams-undecided`), (`rule:nrz:lc-relation-unresolved-implementation`). A stronger pi certificate may settle the same observation family; neither an unavailable proof nor exhaustion authorizes a finite alias cutoff. No fallback executes inside a native lambda.

