**Criterion (LC instantiation acceptance)** · `crit:nrz:lc-evaluation-acceptance`

An implementation satisfies a named slice when its original LC laws, recipe/shape scope, exact evidence, fresh numerical outputs, live attachments, flush behavior and attributed costs meet the linked obligations. Complete LC evaluation requires the full relation, grid and stream acceptance scope under (`rule:nrz:lc-closing-completion`); the initial recipe subset cannot close it, and its standing is recorded in (`sec:nrz:lc-closing-register`). The difficult boundaries are parameterizing ground origins without weakening original targets, proving complete joint alias/fibre coverage, preserving calibrated future quantifiers, and releasing every numerical dependency while authority stays warm. They are explicit capabilities within the decided engine contract, not grounds for changing its cache keys, mask ownership, zero-exact-work kernel boundary, walk, limits or pins. No required engine or concept invariant is waived by this design.
